2026-09-21T17:31:50.385788Z [] {'source_reference_id': 'RFQ-13023050870', 'source_id': 'buynsw', 'title': 'Production Manager ? Music, Minds, Food Vivid Sydney 2027, 2028, 2029', 'issuing_agency': 'Destination NSW', 'category': 'RFQ (Open)', 'status': 'open', 'publish_date': '2026-09-21', 'closing_date': '2026-10-06', 'value_amount': None, 'value_currency': None, 'value_notes': 'Itemised all-inclusive quotation for Vivid Sydney 2027 exclusive of GST but inclusive of all other taxes and charges. The Supplier should quote for the Services based on the scope, whether that be on a daily basis or for the completion of Services required as a whole. A daily rate for additional services not included in the scope of this RFQ should also be provided.', 'location': 'Sydney metro; Sydney CBD; Circular Quay & The Rocks; Barangaroo; Darling Harbour', 'description': 'Destination NSW is seeking a contractor for the role of Production Manager ? Music, Minds, Food for Vivid Sydney 2027, 2028, and 2029. The role involves strategic planning, production and operational management, stakeholder management, budgeting, financial and contract management, procurement, and resourcing for the Vivid Food, Music & Minds operational and production suppliers. Key services include managing budgets, production documentation, project plans, CAD drawings, technical requirements, procurement, event management plans, on-site installation/operation/removal, and contributing to the C4 Event structure. The services are required across Sydney CBD, Circular Quay & The Rocks, Barangaroo, Darling Harbour, and other determined locations.\n\nThe contract is for Vivid Sydney 2027, with options for 2028 and 2029. For Vivid Sydney 2027, the commitment is 3 days per week from 2/11/26 to 24/12/27 (8 weeks) and 5 days per week from 11/1/27 to 9/7/27 (26 weeks). The 2027 event dates are 28 May ? 19 June, with bump-in from 17 May and bump-out from 20 June. Options for 2028 and 2029 have similar weekly commitments but with specific dates to be confirmed; the document lists the 3 days/week period for 2028 as 1/11/26 to 24/12/27 (8 weeks) and 5 days/week as 10/1/27 to 7/7/27 (26 weeks), and for 2029, the 3 days/week period as 30/10/26 to 22/12/27 (8 weeks) and 5 days/week as 8/1/27 to 6/7/27 (26 weeks). The RFQ was published on 21 September 2026, with clarification requests due by 3:00 PM on 28 September 2026. The closing date is 3:00 PM on 6 October 2026, with the successful contractor notified the week commencing 12 October 2026 and contract commencement on 2 November 2026.\n\nRespondents must be legal entities with an ABN and GST registration. This is a contract for services, not employment, and Destination NSW will not accept applications from contingent labour companies. Mandatory insurance requirements include Workers Compensation (as per law), Public Liability of at least $20,000,000 per occurrence, and Professional Indemnity of at least $10,000,000 per occurrence. Respondents must comply with the NSW Supplier Code of Conduct, NSW Procurement Policy Framework, and Modern Slavery Laws. They must also confirm no current or recent legal proceedings, insolvency, or conflicts of interest.\n\nDestination NSW may elect to contract with more than one contractor for the services. The successful contractor will be required to work on-site at Vivid Sydney precincts during bump-in, event, and bump-out periods, including night and weekend shifts. Office facilities (desk, chair, computer, printing, phone, internet) will be provided, but parking is not included. All intellectual property will vest in Destination NSW, and the contract includes a 30-day termination clause without cause. Pricing should be an itemised, all-inclusive quotation for Vivid Sydney 2027, exclusive of GST, with payments based on milestones.', 'summary_headline': 'Destination NSW seeks Production Manager for Vivid Sydney Music, Minds, Food program across 2027, 2028, and 2029.', 'contact_name': 'Bill Harris', 'contact_ema