2026-09-21T17:33:44.054903Z [] {'source_reference_id': 'GO8561', 'source_id': 'grantconnect', 'title': 'Bulk Billing Practices in Central Coast, Newcastle, Lake Macquarie and Hunter Region', 'issuing_agency': 'Department of Health, Disability and Ageing', 'category': 'Grant Opportunity', 'status': 'open', 'publish_date': '2026-09-08', 'closing_date': '2026-09-22', 'value_amount': 24400000.0, 'value_currency': 'AUD', 'value_notes': 'Funding is subject to indexation.', 'location': 'Newcastle, Lower Hunter, Lake Macquarie and Central Coast region, NSW', 'description': 'This is a closed non-competitive grant opportunity for the Hunter New England and Central Coast (HNECC) PHN (ABN 5160 4341 362) to establish six new fully bulk billing general practices in the Newcastle, Lower Hunter, Lake Macquarie, and Central Coast regions of NSW. The HNECC PHN will conduct a commissioning process (e.g., EOI or tender) to select private providers and determine suitable locations for these new practices, ensuring accessibility for those most in need of bulk billed services.\n\nThe total grant funding available is $24.4 million (GST exclusive) over three years, from 2026-27 to 2028-29. This includes $9.9 million for 2026/27, $10 million for 2027/28, and $4.5 million for 2028/29. The maximum grant period is three years, with activities to be completed by 30 June 2029. Funding can be used for initial establishment and operation costs, including minor capital expenditure (fit-out, consumables, medical equipment), initial non-clinical staff, IT, and workforce measures (attracting, relocating, and upskilling GPs). Ineligible expenditures include land purchase, major capital works, retrospective costs, and application preparation.\n\nPractices receiving funding must bulk bill all Medicare-eligible patients (including DVA), register in MyMedicare and the Bulk Billing Practice Incentive Program (BBPIP), advertise their bulk billing status, recruit GPs, and collectively deliver a minimum of 155,000 bulk billed services per year across all six practices. They must also demonstrate a plan for viable, fully bulk billing operations after funding ceases. The grant aims to increase access to affordable healthcare, improve health equity, and attract/retain health workforce in the region, contributing to Closing the Gap targets. The application period is from 8 September 2026 to 2:00 pm (AEST) on 22 September 2026, with questions closing at 5:00 pm (Canberra time) three business days prior. The earliest expected start date for grant activities is November/December 2026.', 'summary_headline': 'Department of Health seeks HNECC PHN to establish six new bulk billing GP clinics in Newcastle, Lower Hunter, Lake Macquarie, and Central Coast.', 'contact_name': None, 'contact_email': 'Grant.ATM@health.gov.au', 'contact_phone': None, 'lodgment_address': 'GrantConnect portal', 'documents': [{'file_name': 'GO8561 - Newcastle - Lower Hunter - Lake Macquarie and Central Coast Bulk Billing Grants Program - Attachment Pack - AWP Budget and Risk.XLSX.txt', 'extracted_text': '## Sheet: 1. AWP\n\tActivity Work Plan (AWP) \t\t\t\t\t\n\t\nGO8561 - Bulk Billing Practices in Central Coast, Newcastle, Lake Macquarie and Hunter Region\t\t\t\t\t\n\tGuidance: Complete the name and ABN of your organisation along with the name you have chosen for the grant activity to be funded under this application process if successful. Complete the below table for the activity/ies covered within your application. Identify the key objectives you are trying to achieve, how you will measure them and timeframes. Complete/add more rows as needed.\t\t\t\t\t\n\t<Insert organisation name and ABN here>\t\t\t\t\t\n\t<Insert the name of your grant activity here>\n<Insert objectives and outcomes here>\t\t\t\t\t\n\tTask(s)\nWhat are you trying to achieve (outcome focused)?\tDeliverable(s)\nWhat will you deliver?\tOutput(s)\nHow much will you deliver?\tPerformance Indicator(s)\nHow will you measure performance?\tTimefr