2026-09-21T17:34:36.161975Z [] {'source_reference_id': '13023050870', 'source_id': 'buynsw', 'title': 'Production Manager ? Music, Minds, Food Vivid Sydney 2027, 2028, 2029', 'issuing_agency': 'Destination NSW', 'category': 'Request for Quotation', 'status': 'open', 'publish_date': '2026-09-21', 'closing_date': '2026-10-06', 'value_amount': None, 'value_currency': None, 'value_notes': 'Itemised all-inclusive quotation for Vivid Sydney 2027 exclusive of GST but inclusive of all other taxes and charges. A daily rate for additional services not included in the scope of this RFQ should also be provided.', 'location': 'Sydney metro; Sydney CBD; Circular Quay & The Rocks; Barangaroo; Darling Harbour', 'description': "Destination NSW (DNSW) is seeking a contractor to fill the role of Production Manager for the Music, Minds, Food program at Vivid Sydney for the 2027, 2028, and 2029 festivals. The scope of work includes strategic planning, production and operational management, stakeholder engagement, budgeting, financial and contract management, procurement, and resourcing for all operational and production suppliers. Key responsibilities involve managing budgets, production documentation, project plans, technical requirements (audio, lighting, vision), event management plans, site infrastructure, and coordinating staff and contractors. The role also contributes to Vivid Sydney's Access & Inclusion and Sustainability initiatives. Services will be required across Sydney CBD, Circular Quay & The Rocks, Barangaroo, Darling Harbour, and other locations.\n\nThe contract term covers Vivid Sydney 2027, with options for 2028 and 2029. For Vivid Sydney 2027, the role requires 3 days per week from 2 November 2026 to 24 December 2027 (8 weeks), increasing to 5 days per week from 11 January 2027 to 9 July 2027 (26 weeks). The festival dates for 2027 are 28 May to 19 June, with bump-in from 17 May and bump-out from 20 June. Similar weekly commitments apply for the option years, with specific dates to be confirmed. The contractor is expected to work a minimum of 3 days per week in the office (typically Mon-Wed), increasing to full-time during peak periods like Program Launch and the festival period. Onsite attendance, including night and weekend shifts, is mandatory during bump-in, the event, and bump-out. DNSW will provide office facilities but not parking. Payment will be milestone-based, not necessarily monthly.\n\nMandatory requirements for respondents include being a legal entity with an Australian Business Number (ABN) and GST registration. Contractors must commit to holding Workers Compensation Insurance (as per law), Public Liability Insurance of no less than $20,000,000 per occurrence, and Professional Indemnity Insurance of no less than $10,000,000 per occurrence. Respondents must comply with the NSW Supplier Code of Conduct, NSW Procurement Policy Framework, and Modern Slavery Laws. Applications from contingent labour companies are not accepted. All intellectual property generated will vest in DNSW. DNSW reserves the right to terminate the contract without cause with 30 days' written notice.\n\nThe RFQ was published on 21 September 2026, with clarification requests due by 3:00 PM on 28 September 2026. The closing date for submissions is 3:00 PM on 6 October 2026. The successful contractor is expected to be notified by 12 October 2026, with the contract commencing on 2 November 2026.", 'summary_headline': 'Destination NSW seeks Production Manager for Vivid Sydney Music, Minds, Food program for 2027, 2028, and 2029.', 'contact_name': 'Bill Harris', 'contact_email': 'Bill.Harris@dnsw.com.au', 'contact_phone': '02 9931 1111', 'lodgment_address': 'Responses must be submitted electronically on the buy NSW Tenders module by a registered user of buy NSW. Uploaded via the NSW Governments tender portal at www.buy.nsw.gov.au.', 'documents': [{'file_name': '20260917-DNSW-Contract-of-Engagement-Template.docx.txt', 'extracted_text': 'OFFICIALOFFICIAL\