2026-09-21T17:36:50.314206Z [] {'source_reference_id': 'GO8561', 'source_id': 'grantconnect', 'title': 'Bulk Billing Practices in Central Coast, Newcastle, Lake Macquarie and Hunter Region', 'issuing_agency': 'Department of Health, Disability and Ageing', 'category': '231018 - Public Health Services', 'status': 'open', 'publish_date': '2026-09-08', 'closing_date': '2026-09-22', 'value_amount': 24400000.0, 'value_currency': 'AUD', 'value_notes': 'Funding is subject to indexation.', 'location': 'NSW, Newcastle, Lower Hunter, Lake Macquarie and Central Coast', 'description': 'The Department of Health, Disability and Ageing is offering a closed non-competitive grant (GO8561) to the Hunter New England and Central Coast (HNECC) PHN to establish six new fully bulk billing General Practitioner (GP) clinics in the Newcastle, Lower Hunter, Lake Macquarie, and Central Coast regions of NSW. HNECC PHN, as the sole eligible applicant, will be responsible for commissioning private providers through its own process (e.g., EOI or competitive tender) and determining suitable clinic locations to ensure accessibility for those most in need.\n\nThe selected private providers will establish and operate these clinics, demonstrating how grant funds will be used for initial establishment and ensuring viable, fully bulk billing operations after funding ceases. Practices must bulk bill all Medicare-eligible patients, register with MyMedicare and the Bulk Billing Practice Incentive Program (BBPIP), advertise their bulk billing status, and collectively deliver a minimum of 155,000 bulk billed services annually across all six new practices. Eligible expenditures include initial capital costs (fit-out, equipment), non-clinical staff, IT infrastructure, and workforce development (GP recruitment, relocation, upskilling).\n\nA total of $24.4 million (GST exclusive) is available for grants over three years, with $9.9 million in 2026/27, $10 million in 2027/28, and $4.5 million in 2028/29. The maximum grant period is three years, with activities to be completed by June 30, 2029. The grant opportunity opened on September 8, 2026, and closes on September 22, 2026, at 2:00 pm AEST. The earliest expected start date for grant activities is November/December 2026.\n\nThis is a highly targeted opportunity for HNECC Limited (ABN 5160 4341 362) only. Applicants must submit an Activity Work Plan, Indicative Activity Budget, and Risk Management Plan. Key performance indicators include establishing six clinics by mid-2027, maintaining BBPIP alignment, and achieving an 85% retention rate for recruited GPs after 12 and 24 months. Compliance with various government frameworks, including Child Safe and Workplace Gender Equality, is mandatory.', 'summary_headline': 'Department of Health seeks HNECC PHN to establish six new bulk billing GP clinics in Newcastle, Lower Hunter, Lake Macquarie, and Central Coast.', 'contact_name': None, 'contact_email': 'Grant.ATM@health.gov.au', 'contact_phone': '1300 484 145', 'lodgment_address': 'via the red Submit Application button on GrantConnect', 'documents': [{'file_name': 'GO8561 - Newcastle - Lower Hunter - Lake Macquarie and Central Coast Bulk Billing Grants Program - Attachment Pack - AWP Budget and Risk.XLSX.txt', 'extracted_text': '## Sheet: 1. AWP\n\tActivity Work Plan (AWP) \t\t\t\t\t\n\t\nGO8561 - Bulk Billing Practices in Central Coast, Newcastle, Lake Macquarie and Hunter Region\t\t\t\t\t\n\tGuidance: Complete the name and ABN of your organisation along with the name you have chosen for the grant activity to be funded under this application process if successful. Complete the below table for the activity/ies covered within your application. Identify the key objectives you are trying to achieve, how you will measure them and timeframes. Complete/add more rows as needed.\t\t\t\t\t\n\t<Insert organisation name and ABN here>\t\t\t\t\t\n\t<Insert the name of your grant activity here>\n<Insert objectives and outcomes here>\t\t\t\t\t\n\t