2026-09-21T17:37:38.580760Z [] {'source_reference_id': '13023050870', 'source_id': 'buynsw', 'title': 'Production Manager ? Music, Minds, Food Vivid Sydney 2027, 2028, 2029', 'issuing_agency': 'Destination NSW', 'category': 'Request for Quotation', 'status': 'open', 'publish_date': '2026-09-21', 'closing_date': '2026-10-06', 'value_amount': None, 'value_currency': None, 'value_notes': 'Itemised all-inclusive quotation for Vivid Sydney 2027 exclusive of GST but inclusive of all other taxes and charges. A daily rate for additional services not included in the scope should also be provided.', 'location': 'Sydney metro; Sydney CBD; Circular Quay & The Rocks; Barangaroo; Darling Harbour; Other locations to be determined at review of service stage', 'description': "Destination NSW (DNSW) is seeking a contractor to fill the role of Production Manager for Music, Minds, and Food events for Vivid Sydney 2027, 2028, and 2029. This is a contract for services, not an employment position, and applications from contingent labour companies are not accepted. The Production Manager will be responsible for strategic planning, project management, production and operational management, stakeholder engagement, budgeting, financial and contract management, procurement, and resourcing for event suppliers. Key services include managing budgets, production documentation, project plans, CAD drawings, technical requirements (audio, lighting, vision), supplier procurement and contract management, event management plans (including WH&S, permits, logistics), on-site installation/operation/removal, staff coordination, and contributing to Access & Inclusion and Sustainability initiatives. Services will be delivered across Sydney CBD, Circular Quay & The Rocks, Barangaroo, Darling Harbour, and other locations.\n\nThe contract covers Vivid Sydney 2027, with options for 2028 and 2029. For Vivid Sydney 2027, the role requires 3 days per week from 2 November 2026 to 24 December 2027 (8 weeks), increasing to 5 days per week from 11 January 2027 to 9 July 2027 (26 weeks). The Vivid Sydney 2027 event dates are 28 May to 19 June 2027, with bump-in from 17 May and bump-out from 20 June. The RFQ was published on 21 September 2026, with clarification requests due by 3:00 PM on 28 September 2026. Responses close at 3:00 PM on 6 October 2026. The successful contractor is expected to be notified the week commencing 12 October 2026, with contract commencement on 2 November 2026.\n\nRespondents must be a legal entity with an ABN and GST registration. Mandatory insurance requirements include Public Liability Insurance of no less than $20,000,000 per occurrence, Workers Compensation Insurance, and Professional Indemnity Insurance of no less than $10,000,000 per occurrence. The contractor must comply with relevant Modern Slavery and Child Protection legislation. DNSW will provide office facilities, but parking is not included. The role requires a minimum of three days per week in the office, increasing to full-time during peak periods and on-site attendance during bump-in, event, and bump-out, which will include night and weekend shifts. DNSW retains ownership of all intellectual property created under the contract and can terminate the agreement with 30 days' notice.", 'summary_headline': 'Destination NSW seeks Production Manager for Music, Minds, Food events at Vivid Sydney 2027, 2028, and 2029.', 'contact_name': 'Bill Harris', 'contact_email': 'Bill.Harris@dnsw.com.au', 'contact_phone': '02 9931 1111', 'lodgment_address': 'Submitted electronically on the buy NSW Tenders module / NSW Governments tender portal at www.buy.nsw.gov.au.', 'documents': [{'file_name': '20260917-DNSW-Contract-of-Engagement-Template.docx.txt', 'extracted_text': 'OFFICIALOFFICIAL\nOFFICIALOFFICIAL\nL\\353550838.1OFFICIALOFFICIAL\nL\\353550838.1OFFICIALOFFICIAL\nPARTY DETAILS\nParties\nDestination NSW\nLevel 2, 88 Cumberland Street, The Rocks, NSW, 2000\nABN: 52 890 768 976\n(Destination NSW or DNSW)\nan