2026-09-21T17:39:51.856667Z [] {'source_reference_id': 'GO8561', 'source_id': 'grantconnect', 'title': 'Bulk Billing Practices in Central Coast, Newcastle, Lake Macquarie and Hunter Region', 'issuing_agency': 'Department of Health, Disability and Ageing', 'category': '231018 - Public Health Services', 'status': None, 'publish_date': '2026-09-08', 'closing_date': '2026-09-22', 'value_amount': 24400000.0, 'value_currency': 'AUD', 'value_notes': 'Total $24.4 million is available for grants over three years from 2026-27 to 2028-29. Funding is subject to indexation.', 'location': 'Newcastle, Lower Hunter, Lake Macquarie and Central Coast', 'description': 'The Department of Health, Disability and Ageing is offering a closed non-competitive grant (GO8561) to the Hunter New England and Central Coast (HNECC) Primary Health Network (PHN) to establish six new fully bulk billing general practices in the Newcastle, Lower Hunter, Lake Macquarie, and Central Coast regions of NSW. HNECC PHN is the sole eligible applicant and will be responsible for commissioning private providers and determining suitable practice locations through its own competitive process.\n\nThe objective is to increase access to affordable bulk billed GP services and attract/retain health workforce in the region. Private providers selected by HNECC PHN will establish and operate these clinics, committing to bulk bill all Medicare-eligible patients, register with MyMedicare and the Bulk Billing Practice Incentive Program (BBPIP), and deliver a minimum of 155,000 bulk billed services annually across all six practices. Funding can cover initial establishment and operational costs, including minor capital, IT, staff recruitment, relocation, and training. Excluded expenditures include land purchase, major capital works, and retrospective costs.\n\nA total of $24.4 million (GST exclusive) is available over three years, from 2026-27 to 2028-29, with $9.9 million in 2026/27, $10 million in 2027/28, and $4.5 million in 2028/29. The grant period is three years, with activities to be completed by 30 June 2029. The application period for HNECC PHN is from 8 September 2026 to 2:00 pm (AEST) on 22 September 2026, with an expected activity start date of November/December 2026.\n\nThis is a targeted grant, meaning only HNECC PHN (ABN: 5160 4341 362) can apply, leveraging their existing infrastructure and regional expertise. The grant also aims to contribute to "Closing the Gap" targets related to life expectancy and digital inclusion for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Applicants must submit an Activity Work Plan, Indicative Activity Budget, and Risk Management Plan as mandatory attachments.', 'summary_headline': 'Department of Health seeks to establish six new bulk billing GP clinics in Newcastle, Lower Hunter, Lake Macquarie, and Central Coast.', 'contact_name': None, 'contact_email': 'Grant.ATM@health.gov.au', 'contact_phone': '1300 484 145', 'lodgment_address': 'Submit via the red Submit Application button on GrantConnect', 'documents': [{'file_name': 'GO8561 - Newcastle - Lower Hunter - Lake Macquarie and Central Coast Bulk Billing Grants Program - Attachment Pack - AWP Budget and Risk.XLSX.txt', 'extracted_text': '## Sheet: 1. AWP\n\tActivity Work Plan (AWP) \t\t\t\t\t\n\t\nGO8561 - Bulk Billing Practices in Central Coast, Newcastle, Lake Macquarie and Hunter Region\t\t\t\t\t\n\tGuidance: Complete the name and ABN of your organisation along with the name you have chosen for the grant activity to be funded under this application process if successful. Complete the below table for the activity/ies covered within your application. Identify the key objectives you are trying to achieve, how you will measure them and timeframes. Complete/add more rows as needed.\t\t\t\t\t\n\t<Insert organisation name and ABN here>\t\t\t\t\t\n\t<Insert the name of your grant activity here>\n<Insert objectives and outcomes here>\t\t\t\t\t\n\tTask(s)\nWhat are you trying to achieve (outcome f