2026-09-21T17:40:41.544279Z [] {'source_reference_id': 'RFQ-13023050870', 'source_id': 'buynsw', 'title': 'Production Manager ? Music, Minds, Food Vivid Sydney 2027, 2028, 2029', 'issuing_agency': 'Destination NSW', 'category': 'Request for Quotation', 'status': 'open', 'publish_date': '2026-09-21', 'closing_date': '2026-10-06', 'value_amount': None, 'value_currency': None, 'value_notes': 'Itemised all-inclusive quotation for Vivid Sydney 2027 exclusive of GST but inclusive of all other taxes and charges. A daily rate for additional services not included in the scope should also be provided.', 'location': 'Sydney metro; Sydney CBD; Circular Quay & The Rocks; Barangaroo; Darling Harbour; Other locations to be determined at review of service stage', 'description': 'Destination NSW is seeking a contractor to fill the role of Production Manager ? Music, Minds, Food for the Vivid Sydney festival across the 2027, 2028, and 2029 editions. This is a contract for services, not a direct employment position, and applications from contingent labour companies are explicitly not accepted. The role involves strategic planning, project and operational management, stakeholder engagement, budgeting, financial and contract management, and procurement for the Vivid Food, Music & Minds programs. Key services include managing production documentation, event plans, technical requirements (audio, lighting, vision), supplier contracts, and on-site delivery across various Sydney locations including Sydney CBD, Circular Quay, The Rocks, Barangaroo, and Darling Harbour.\n\nThe contract for Vivid Sydney 2027 runs from 2 November 2026 to 9 July 2027, with an initial 8 weeks at 3 days per week (2/11/26 ? 24/12/27) and then 26 weeks at 5 days per week (11/1/27 ? 9/7/27). The Vivid Sydney 2027 event dates are 28 May ? 19 June 2027. Options exist for contract renewal for Vivid Sydney 2028 and 2029, with similar work schedules. The successful contractor is expected to work a minimum of three days per week in the DNSW office, increasing to full-time during peak periods like Program Launch and the festival itself, including on-site attendance during bump-in, event, and bump-out periods, which will involve night and weekend shifts.\n\nMandatory requirements include being a legal entity with an ABN and GST registration, holding Public Liability Insurance of no less than $20,000,000 per occurrence, Professional Indemnity Insurance of no less than $10,000,000 per occurrence, and Workers Compensation Insurance as per law. Respondents must comply with NSW Procurement Board Directions, Policies, Codes, and Standards, and the NSW Supplier Code of Conduct. The Request for Quotation (RFQ) was published on 21 September 2026, with a deadline for clarification requests by 3:00 PM on 28 September 2026. Responses must be submitted via the Buy NSW website by 3:00 PM on 6 October 2026. The successful contractor is expected to be notified the week commencing 12 October 2026, with the contract commencing on 2 November 2026. Destination NSW retains ownership of all intellectual property created under the contract and has a 30-day termination clause without cause.', 'summary_headline': 'Destination NSW seeks Production Manager for Music, Minds, Food events at Vivid Sydney 2027, 2028, and 2029.', 'contact_name': 'Bill Harris', 'contact_email': 'Bill.Harris@dnsw.com.au', 'contact_phone': '02 9931 1111', 'lodgment_address': 'Submitted electronically on the buy NSW Tenders module via the NSW Governments tender portal at www.buy.nsw.gov.au.', 'documents': [{'file_name': '20260917-DNSW-Contract-of-Engagement-Template.docx.txt', 'extracted_text': 'OFFICIALOFFICIAL\nOFFICIALOFFICIAL\nL\\353550838.1OFFICIALOFFICIAL\nL\\353550838.1OFFICIALOFFICIAL\nPARTY DETAILS\nParties\nDestination NSW\nLevel 2, 88 Cumberland Street, The Rocks, NSW, 2000\nABN: 52 890 768 976\n(Destination NSW or DNSW)\nand\n[Supplier name]\n[Insert registered address]\nABN/ACN/International Business Number \n(Supplier)\nCONT